There is no registration, activation, license-server connection or reporting
requirement for free permitted use. The Software contains no license-enforcement
telemetry required by this license. Making a permitted modification does not
require publishing your own application's source code.

3. Qualifying Small Business

A business qualifies only while BOTH of the following are true:

(a) its Group Revenue is less than USD 1,000,000 for the immediately preceding
    twelve months; and
(b) its Group Headcount is fewer than 25 people.

A business includes a self-employed person or sole proprietor when acting for
commercial purposes. Group means the business and all entities controlling,
controlled by, or under common control with it. Control means holding more than
50 percent of voting rights or having the power to direct management. A small
team, department, project or subsidiary inside a larger group is not measured
separately.

Group Revenue is consolidated gross revenue from all business activities before
expenses and taxes, excluding sales/VAT taxes collected for governments and
intra-group transactions. Equity investment, loan proceeds and charitable
donations are not revenue for this test. For a business younger than twelve
months, use actual revenue since formation without annualizing it. Convert
non-USD revenue using a consistently applied, publicly documented central-bank
average exchange rate for the measured period.

Group Headcount is the number of employees plus individual contractors working
for the group, counted once per person. Count people, not software users or
developer seats. A contractor using the Software solely on behalf of a customer
must assess that customer's group as well as the contractor's own business;
both must qualify unless the customer's commercial agreement covers that use.

4. Crossing a threshold

A previously qualifying business receives one transition period of 90 calendar
days from the first date either threshold is reached. Its existing and new use
may continue under this license during that period. At its end, continuing
production business use requires a written commercial license. A business that
already exceeds either threshold when it first uses the Software has no
production transition period, but may evaluate under section 2(d).

There are no retroactive fees for use that was permitted at the time. The
transition period cannot be restarted by reorganizing a group or temporarily
reducing revenue or headcount. A business that subsequently qualifies again may
resume permitted use, but does not receive a second transition period.

